id: pm-reopen-planning-recovery
title: Expose active planning recovery when a canonical item is reopened
description: "Normal item reopen archives and clears expected_result, then claim --start accepts the item while active tracker assurance requires a nonempty expected result. The current reopen help offers only its own help example and no planning recovery. Add SDK-owned structured recovery or a declared explicit planning input that lets an operator restore the intended active expected result while preserving immutable previous-terminal evidence."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T05:28:30.227Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T06:54:43.630Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-12T06:54:42.674Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-12T06:54:42.674Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Real isolated reopen/claim/help journey discloses the required planning recovery; explicit current expectation is preserved; previous terminal fields remain immutable in history; existing active metadata gates remain unchanged
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make recurrence reopening disclose the active planning prerequisite
value: Self-improvement iterations remain actionable and pass existing planning assurance
why_now: Canonical publication guard recurrence twice cleared expected_result and the static gate correctly refused until explicit planning was restored
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Accept and preserve the current SDK/CLI/MCP expectation during reopening, advertise same-tracker recovery when omitted, and explicitly document that the old expectation is cleared while a newly supplied value survives."
expected_result: "Reopen users can distinguish archived prior expectations from the active expectation they explicitly supplied, without weaker planning assurance."
actual_result: Existing reopening implementation and transport regressions remain unchanged from their passing linked receipts. The corrected documentation passes build and the docs/skills link gate; focused review validation passes72 tests. Earlier close/reopen context remains immutable.
