comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-11T05:28:30.227Z","harness:codex","Duplicate intake: request-specific live reopen/expected searches, strict complete2924-item all-status corpus, current open/in-progress lists, full closed reopen lineage and live reopen help found no focused owner for active planning recovery. Completed clear-terminal implementation remains completed. This enhancement is open and unclaimed; no source work is started."
  "2026-10-11T22:43:59.439Z","harness:codex","Additional dogfood recurrence during PR #1444 / pm-9djr6d: normal reopen archived and cleared expected_result, claim --start succeeded, and the unchanged canonical static tracker gate then failed active-missing-expected-result-zero with pm-9djr6d as its only contributor. The current acceptance criterion was restored with pm update --expected-result before rerunning. Full live owner/history verification confirms this existing open, unclaimed task owns the recovery enhancement; no duplicate item or additional in-progress claim was created. Preserve previous-terminal evidence while advertising the planning restoration step."
  "2026-10-12T03:33:38.734Z","harness:codex","SDK, CLI and generic MCP dispatch preserve an explicit current expectedResult atomically while retaining the prior terminal expectation in immutable recurrence context. Without input, the compact receipt advertises a same-tracker update argument vector; its placeholder is replaced and executed in isolated tests and installed Node/Bun consumers. Blank explicit expectations refuse before history writes. Current help advertises the planning prerequisite and examples. Public optional-field signature changes carry a reviewed compatibility rationale; unchanged active metadata gates remain enforced."
  "2026-10-12T05:00:39.170Z","harness:codex","The new real CLI transport assertion exposed an actual alias gap: declaring --expected in the runtime contract did not register it on the nested item-reopen Commander node. The thin adapter now registers the alias and forwards it with canonical-option precedence. Source-level adapter tests verify canonical and alias options, while the isolated real CLI journey verifies the alias writes the active expectation and archives the earlier terminal value. This is a transport correction, not a relaxed coverage gate or removal of advertised functionality."
  "2026-10-12T05:35:01.332Z","harness:codex","Final acceptance: both linked SDK/reopen and source CLI adapter commands pass with immutable test_runs evidence. Exact whole-source coverage is 100/100/100/100; SDK contracts, surface snapshot, four-project TypeScript and transport gates pass. Fresh packed Node and Bun clients verify explicit expectation, immutable prior-terminal expectation and execution of the advertised same-tracker update recovery. Both canonical and --expected alias transports pass; blank explicit input refuses before mutation. These optional SDK additions remain a source candidate until reviewed merge and the next daily publication."
  "2026-10-12T05:49:43.868Z","harness:codex","Reviewed delivery: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1445 carries the verified optional planning input, executable recovery, public SDK/MCP contracts and canonical/short CLI flags with structured closure evidence. Current-head checks and bot review remain pending; next daily publication is separate."
  "2026-10-12T06:54:41.781Z","harness:codex","PR1445 inline4245053340 addressed: documentation now separately names cleared prior terminal fields and the newly supplied current expectation that survives. Existing functional reopen code is unchanged. The focused build and all72 merge/risk/diagnostic tests pass, and the focused docs/skills link gate passes; prior linked reopen/adapter receipts remain valid for the unchanged logic."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T03:06:14.623Z","harness:codex","SDK compatibility review: expectedResult and recovery are optional additions. Existing reopen calls still archive terminal fields and return recurrence evidence; an explicit current expectation is written atomically with reopen. The conservative public-surface signature gate requires a recorded rationale for interface changes even when fields are optional. Consume these changes in the next eligible calendar release, preserving existing immutable daily artifacts."
  "2026-10-12T05:05:43.824Z","harness:codex","Linked-test command identity is immutable: the attempted command-field edit was refused with no mutation. Keep the original SDK/reopen journey link and add the distinct CLI adapter suite as a separate runnable link. This preserves original command provenance and avoids unsupported delete/recreate or identity rewriting."
